# ── Configuration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Edit config.py directly instead of using .env files.
# All settings have sensible defaults; only change what you need.
#
# Quick-start (Docker):
#   1. Edit config.py and set WILDDUCK_API_URL / TOKEN / ADMIN_PASSWORD.
#   2. docker compose up -d
#
# Quick-start (local):
#   1. Edit config.py with your WildDuck API details.
#   2. pip install -r requirements.txt
#   3. python app.py
#
# Environment variables can still override config.py values at runtime
# (useful in Docker / Kubernetes without rebuilding the image):
#
#   WILDDUCK_API_URL    – WildDuck REST API base URL
#   WILDDUCK_API_TOKEN  – API access token (X-Access-Token header)
#   ADMIN_USERNAME      – Panel login username
#   ADMIN_PASSWORD      – Panel login password (bcrypt-hashed at startup)
#   FLASK_SECRET_KEY    – Flask session signing key
#   FLASK_DEBUG         – Set to "true" for debug mode
